:: Haegish Intro
<<npc "Haegish">><<person1>>
You approach the long table lying on the yellow greenish grass of the grove. An older <<personsimple>> sits at the head of the table, a large hat covered in small melting clocks adorns <<his>> head, split by two large rabbit ears. Tufts of whispy white hair stick out from under the hat at odd angles framing <<his>> portly frame. Adorning <<his>> body are several gold trinkets pinned to <<his>> tidy red suit.
<br><br>
<span class = "orange">"Ah! Ah! Another person! How delightfully unpredictable!"</span> The <<personsimple>> claps <<his>> hands once, sharp and succinct. <span class = "orange">"You know, I once tried to host a tea party for a crocodile who insisted he was actually a very confused badger in a waistcoat. Terrible etiquette darling. Terrible."</span> <<He>> leans in conspiratorially, eyes glinting. <span class = "orange">"But you, my dear, you radiate the essence of a late afternoon. Exactly three minutes past six, if my watch weren't broken, which it is, of course. Always broken. Time's terribly rude to watches, you see."</span> <<He>> pulls a broken watch from <<his>> red suit pocket and stares at the frozen hands.
<br><br>
He begins to pace in a tight circle, muttering to <<himself>> before turning <<his>> red eyes back to you. <span class = "yellow">"You! Yes, you! Are you ready for some tea? Or perhaps, a lesson in pleasantries? Around here, we celebrate holidays every day! Far superior to boring old holidays. Presents every day, right boys?! Except today, apparently. Today is... none of your holidays. How utterly tragic."</span> <<He>> says looking disappointedly at the empty chairs.
<br><br>
The <<personsimple>> suddenly stops pacing, head tilting like a curious bird. <<his>> expression shifts to one of sudden sincerity. <span class = "green">"You know... I once knew a girl who sold rabbit pelts on rainy days near the shore. She said the ocean whispered secrets. I told her secrets were for teapots. She laughed, then she left. Left me with only the whisper of the wind in the cotton, and the dreadful suspicion that I'd forgotten how to be sunny."</span> <<his>> voice drops, losing its manic edge for a fragile second.
<br><br>
<<He>> snaps back to grinning mania just as quickly, snapping <<his>> fingers. <span class = "purple">"But enough of that! Dirty cups! Dirty cups! Let's all move down two places! Except you. You stay. You're the guest of honor. Oh where are my manners, it slipped my mind! My name is Haegish but they call me the Dirty Lobster, pleased to acquaint you."</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Haegish Grove]]>><<set $haegishintro to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>


:: Haegish Grove
<<npc "Haegish">><<person1>>
You are in a mushroom filled luminous grove filled with a large table spanning several meters. Haegish laughs to <<himself>> quietly to a joke only <<he>> can hear.
<br><br>
<<link [[Take a seat|Haegish Speak]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Fae Realm]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Haegish Speak
<<npc "Haegish">><<person1>>
Haegish's head snaps upright at the sound of the chair scraping. <span class = "pink">"Sat down! Marvelous! Absolutely riveting!"</span> <<He>> claps again. <<He>> grabs a teapot that floats midair, pouring invisible liquid into three mismatched cups. <span class = "pink">"Cup of existential dread? Or perhaps a spot of suntime memories? No pressure! Except there's always pressure. Especially in teapots. Terrible design flaw, really. Should've gone with soup."</span>
<br><br>
<<He>> slides a cup toward you, steam curling into shapes that resemble rabbits. <span class = "red">"Drink up!"</span> <<his>> voice drops, suddenly close to your ear, smelling of lemon peel. <span class = "red">"Do you ever feel like you're just a spoon stirring someone else's tea?... Pass the sugar, would you?"</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask how <<he>> got here|Haegish How]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
<<if $haegishquest is undefined>>
	<<link [[Ask if <<he>> needs help|Haegish Help]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif $haegishquest is 1 or $haegishquest is 2>>
	<<link [[Return to Haegish about the quest|Haegish Return]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<elseif $haegishquest is 3>>
	<<link [[Ask Haegish about the watch|Haegish Watch]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave|Fae Realm]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Haegish How
<<npc "Haegish">><<person1>>
<span class = "blue">"Got here? Got here?"</span> A high laugh escapes <<him>>. He whirls, hat askew, one rabbit ear twitching toward the distant sound of a nonexistent bell. <span class = "blue">"Why, I tumbled! Fell clean through the bottom of my own teacup last Tuesday! Or was it next Thursday? Time's turned its back on me again, rude thing, always showing up late to its own funeral."</span>
<br><br>
It seems like it would be impossible to get anything meaningful out of <<him>>. <<He>> has clearly lost it and nothing <<he>> says is reliable.
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Fae Realm]]>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Haegish Help
<<npc "Haegish">><<person1>>
<span class = "teal">"Do I look like I need help, little penguin?"</span> A boisterous laugh escapes <<his>> belly. <span class = "teal">"Though if the young flower leaf wishes to fall who can stop it?"</span> Haegish pauses to think for a moment. <span class = "teal">"Ah that's it! That's it! This one requires more tea for the kettle. Bring the finest tea in the wilds and you will get my special blessing! Now shoo, now shoo! The pot won't fill itself!... Will it?"</span> <<He>> pauses to contemplate as you back away from the table. You wonder what this <<personsimple>> has to offer worth getting.
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Fae Realm]]>><<set $haegishquest to 1>><<npcincr Haegish love 10>><<endevent>><</link>>

:: Haegish Return
<<npc "Haegish">><<person1>>
<<if $haegishquest is 2>>
	<span class = "lightpurple">"Oh my, oh my! You have found some tea? Why you shouldn't have! Seriously, who asked you to get this stuff?"</span> <<He>> tosses the jar of tea leaves into the treeline. <span class = "lightpurple">"But since you did such a nice deed without me even asking, why don't I give you something special!"</span> Haegish removes a small slightly melted silver stopwatch from <<his>> pocket. <span class = "lightpurple">"Here for you dear, don't spend it all in one place."</span> <<He>> chuckles loudly and smacks his belly. <span class = "lightpurple">"Now run along little scamp!"</span>
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Leave|Fae Realm]]>><<set $haegishquest to 3>><<npcincr Haegish love 10>><<endevent>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<span class = "gold">"You're back already?! Why I don't see any tea whatsoever! Come back once you have some tea for the party or the guests will go thirsty!"</span> Haegish jestures a plump hand toward the empty seats. <span class = "gold">"We wouldn't want the guests to go thirsty now do we?!"</span> <<He>> lets out a boisterous laugh. It would probably be better to only come back with the tea he requested.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Leave|Fae Realm]]>><<set $haegishquest to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Haegish Watch
<<npc "Haegish">><<person1>>
<<set V.transformationParts.bunny.ears to "default">>
<<set V.transformationParts.bunny.tail to "default">>
<<set V.transformationParts.traits.kicks to "default">>
<<set $bunnytf to 1>>
<<set $permanentTransform to 1>>
<span class = "lightpink">"A watch?! Why what watch could you ever mean? This one? Or perhaps this one? Or... this one?"</span> Haegish begins to pull watches from under <<his>> hat, <<his>> coat pocket, and even <<his>> sock. You stop him and show the watch <<he>> gave you. <span class = "lightpink">"Wow, that is a nice watch! Quite the nice watch. Where did you get it? I would give you something nice in exchange for such a great stopwatch!"</span> <<He>> pats down <<his>> pockets before displaying a disheartened frown. <span class = "lightpink">"Well it seems I may have misplaced my valuables. I was sure I left my ambidexterous musician goose in my pocket!"</span> 
<br><br>
<<He>> frantically searches <<his>> pockets over and over again before pausing. <span class = "orange">"Oh right here it is!"</span> Haegish pulls down a floating jar and inside is a tiny goose playing a trumpet. <<He>> places the tiny goose in your hand. <span class = "orange">"That should do it, now would you give me that quite superb and dare I say delicious watch?"</span>
<br><br>
Haegish pauses as it seems like you want something more. <span class = "red">"Then... perhaps I can teach you something I once learned from an old friend of mine. He was a fanciful frog in a suit, quite a dashing gentleman. But here let me show you the trick!"</span> Haegish grips your stopwatch and places <<his>> hand over yours. You feel a sense of disconnect as the world tilts slightly. A strange feeling fills you as you suddenly grow a pair of long soft ears and a soft cotton tail.
<br><br>
<span class = "green">"And there you have it. What do you think? Now you look quite fanciful yourself my soft bunny friend."</span> <<He>> lets out a loud laugh as <<he>> rubs your ears and takes the watch. <span class = "green">Take care! Take care! Hope to see you upon the bicycles return to the beginning, or was it the end.</span> <<He>> becomes lost in thought as you step back.
<br><br>
<<link [[Leave|Fae Realm]]>><<set $haegishquest to 4>><<npcincr Haegish love 10>><<endevent>><</link>>